    "field": "Aerosol-climate interactions",
    "problem": "This study addresses the challenge of quantifying the climate response to future aerosol pollution reduction strategies, as these efforts to improve air quality may inadvertently amplify global warming by removing the cooling effect of aerosols that masks some greenhouse gas-induced warming.",
    "method": "We use the global atmospheric GCM ECHAM5-HAM to perform equilibrium simulations assessing the climate impact of a maximum feasible aerosol abatement scenario for 2030, investigating its effects both separately from and in combination with increasing greenhouse gas concentrations.",
    "task": "The task is to use a global climate model to assess the impacts of future air pollution mitigation strategies on climate, specifically investigating maximum feasible aerosol reductions by 2030 in combination with increasing greenhouse gas concentrations.",
    "model": [
        "ECHAM5-HAM"
    ],
